  "reading": "compliance (positive one-sided evidence DEV rate is BELOW chance/artifact nulls, Holm-Bonferroni corrected across the 3 years, in every year)",
  "interpretation": "H2_SUPPORTED=True means: in every one of the three independent NIS years, Excludes1-incompatible DX1/secondary-diagnosis pairs occurred SIGNIFICANTLY LESS OFTEN than both the chance-co-occurrence and coding-artifact nulls predict (one-sided tests, Holm-Bonferroni corrected across years), and this pattern was stable across years. H2_SUPPORTED=False can mean any of three different things - check per_year_outcome and any_year_against_H2/any_year_inconclusive/any_year_underpowered to see which: (1) at least one year showed a rate SIGNIFICANTLY ABOVE chance (evidence AGAINST H2, a distinct and more serious finding than inconclusive), (2) at least one year was INCONCLUSIVE (failed to reject either one-sided null - absence of evidence, not evidence of absence; check any_year_underpowered - with n_permutations this small the test may simply lack power), or (3) the temporal-stability criterion failed even though every year individually supported H2. These are NOT interchangeable and must be reported separately, not collapsed into one negative verdict.",
  "note": "All stability/negative-control thresholds and alpha in config.yaml are unverified placeholders pending literature-derived or committee-approved benchmarks - this verdict is only as trustworthy as those thresholds. A low/absent DEV rate is evidence of Excludes1-consistent CODING, not proof of diagnostic accuracy - Excludes1 compliance and correct diagnosis are different claims. This is a hospitalization-level test restricted to the 15 studied phenotypes as DX1, not a claim about all NIS principal diagnoses."
